From cf7a87a72029dba07756c9ae4b56c2b328540c74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guan Xuetao <gxt@pku.edu.cn>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 03:12:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] target/dadao: Add DADAO target skeleton

Add DADAO CPU target skeleton for QEMU. This includes:
- target/dadao/: CPU state (rd/rb/rf/ra[64], pc), QOM registration,
  TCG translation skeleton (all instructions trigger ILLI), helpers
- hw/dadao/: M1 bare-metal machine (RAM 16MiB, ROM 64KiB, exit port
  with qemu_system_shutdown_request_with_code for exit code propagation)
- configs/targets/dadao-softmmu.mak: target configuration
- configs/devices/dadao-softmmu/default.mak: device configuration
- Build system integration: target/meson.build, target/Kconfig,
  hw/meson.build (subdir('dadao')), hw/Kconfig, qapi/machine.json
  (SysEmuTarget), include/qemu/base-arch-defs.h (QEMU_ARCH_DADAO)

Memory map per ADR-0004 D1:
  RAM:        0xffff_0000_0000 (16 MiB)
  Exit port:  0xffff_8000_0000 (8 B)
  Boot ROM:   0xffff_ffff_0000 (64 KiB)

Reset values per ADR-0004 D2:
  rb0/pc = 0xffff_ffff_0000 (boot ROM base)
  rf0    = 0x7FF8_0000_7FC0_0000 (FCSR, derived from SimRISC-00)

All instructions default to gen_exception_illegal() (ILLI).
Big-endian instruction fetch and data access.
Machine name: dadao-m1
